---
title: Docs — Knowledge Islands
description: "Every guide the site publishes, grouped into sections you can work through, followed by the catalogue of every public project in the ecosystem."
permalink: /docs/
layout: layouts/base.njk
---
{% from "macros/icons.njk" import kiIcon %}
{%- set allDocs = collections.docsPages -%}

<section class="section-navy hero-section hero-section-standard">
  <div class="page-container" style="max-width: 64rem;">
    <p class="overline-gold">Documentation</p>
    <h1 class="heading-display-light" style="font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4vw, 3.25rem); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; max-width: 24ch;">Pick an island and work through it.</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 1.125rem; color: rgb(245 239 224 / 75%); max-width: 58ch; line-height: 1.7;">Each section below is a finite body of material with a beginning and an end. The page count is on the card, so you know what you are agreeing to before you start. Begin at Get Started, or go straight to whatever you came for.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-parchment section-pad">
  <div class="page-container" style="max-width: 64rem;">
    <div class="grid-2col" style="gap: 1.5rem;">

{%- for section in docsSections %}
  {#- Count and entry point are derived from the pages that actually carry this
      section's binding, never declared, so a card cannot claim a number the
      section does not hold (KI-WEBSITE-SITE-037). -#}
  {%- set pages = [] -%}
  {%- for page in allDocs %}
    {%- if page.data.section == section.slug %}{% set pages = (pages.push(page), pages) %}{% endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
  {%- if pages.length %}
      <a href="{{ pages[0].url }}" class="card-ki tool-card" style="color: inherit; text-decoration: none;">
        <p class="overline">{{ pages.length }} page{% if pages.length != 1 %}s{% endif %}</p>
        <h2 class="card-title">{{ section.title }}</h2>
        <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: 0.9375rem; margin: 0;">{{ section.description }}</p>
        <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; margin: 0.625rem 0 0;">Start at {{ pages[0].data.title }} →</p>
      </a>
  {%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-mist section-pad" id="catalogue">
  <div class="page-container" style="max-width: 64rem;">
    <div class="prose-ki" style="max-width: none; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <p class="overline">The catalogue</p>
      <h2>Every public project, and what it is the authority for.</h2>
      <p>The sections above answer <em>how do I</em>. This catalogue answers <em>what is this</em>: every repository in the ecosystem, with what it owns and where it lives. Each card opens the project's own page; <a href="/projects/">Projects</a> holds the same catalogue grouped by kind, with a word on each group.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-2col" style="gap: 1.5rem;">
  {#- Rendered from the same project registry /projects/index.njk reads, card for card, so the
      catalogue here and the directory there cannot list different projects. -#}
  {%- for project in projects %}
      <a href="{{ project.route | default('/projects/' + project.slug + '/') }}" class="card-ki tool-card" style="color: inherit; text-decoration: none;">
        <div class="symbol-circle symbol-circle-{{ project.accent }}">{{ kiIcon(project.icon, 22) }}</div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.625rem;"><code>{{ project.name }}</code></h3>
        <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: 0.9375rem; margin: 0;">{{ project.tagline }}</p>
        {%- if project.version %}
        <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; margin: 0.625rem 0 0;">{{ project.version }} · {{ project.maturity }}</p>
        {%- else %}
        <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; margin: 0.625rem 0 0;">{{ project.availability }}{% if project.route %} · {{ project.route }}{% endif %}</p>
        {%- endif %}
      </a>
  {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-parchment section-pad">
  <div class="page-container" style="max-width: 64rem;">
    <div class="prose-ki" style="max-width: none;">
      <p class="overline">What is not here</p>
      <h2>The catalogue is a directory, not a section.</h2>
      <p>The catalogue below the sections, and <a href="/projects/">Projects</a>, list every repository in the ecosystem with what it owns and where it lives. They answer <em>what is this</em>. The sections above answer <em>how do I</em>, which is a different question with a different home: nothing in the catalogue is a guide, and no guide lives under a project.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
